        "created_at": "2018-06-24T12:39:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I listened to this episode just now, and unfortunately I don't have anything insteresting to comment on Young Legacy. Her solo series sounds cool and it'd be the kind of thing I'd like to read in my own college years (but not as much as Tome of the Bizarre).</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I'm loving the Daybreak stuff we got to see. Muse is probably my favorite due to the creepy theme and being interested on the Dreamer-as-a-hero concept since Quando-Ahora, but Muerto looks so friggin cool that I can't decide anymore.&nbsp;</p><p>And I don't know what you guys are talking about, Aeon Girl is adorable. \"Oh but she looks a inhuman creature that doesn't know human emotions and can probably cause unimaginable destruction\", yeah and this only adds to the cuteness.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>But the thing that most called my attention was the mention of Time Slinger as a character in Daybreak. I mean, lots of characters are probably going to appear in Daybreak stories as teachers and special appearances, but the way C&amp;A talked it seemed like Jim would be a important recurring character. It's nice to know, specially since I was afraid he'd be kind of forgotten after Oblivaeon (with time-travel not existing anymore and whatnot), only appearing as a background character in big events.&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
